E["npc:archmage-ansirem-runeweaver"] = {t="npc",n="Archmage Ansirem Runeweaver",z="alterac",s="Archmage Ansirem Runeweaver is a senior human wizard and a ruling member of Dalaran's Council of Six. Having survived the Scourge's destruction of Dalaran in the Third War, he oversees Kirin Tor operations from the Violet Citadel as Dalaran is rebuilt. Though dedicated to the rebuilding of his city, he also maintains discreet interests abroad—including a willful daughter who ran off to Booty Bay to become a pirate.",h="Archmage Ansirem Runeweaver is a senior human wizard and a ruling member of Dalaran's Council of Six.",sec={{t="A Pillar of the Kirin Tor",b="A veteran mage who helped defend Dalaran across decades, Ansirem Runeweaver sits on the Council of Six, the ruling magocracy of the Kirin Tor. He survived the devastation when Arthas Menethil and the Scourge marched upon the city and Archimonde was summoned. In the wake of Dalaran's fall, Ansirem has aided the efforts to rebuild the arcane city, whose protective shield was lifted early, and now works from the Violet Citadel.",sp=0},{t="Far-Flung Interests",b="Despite his scholarly duties and stern wizardly demeanor, Ansirem possesses personal ties far beyond the Alterac Mountains. His willful daughter, Catelyn, ran off to Booty Bay to become a pirate, taking with her an ancient troll dagger he had found while researching in Stranglethorn. He has also dealt with Baron Revilgaz there. He has also engaged in arcane studies involving troll antiquities and maintains diplomatic conduits across distant realms.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Archmage Ansirem Runeweaver?",a="He is an accomplished human wizard and one of the six ruling archmages on the Kirin Tor's Council of Six. He has spent decades defending Dalaran and now oversees operations surrounding the reconstructed city and its arcane perimeter.",al={"who is ansirem","ansirem runeweaver lore","who is the archmage"}},{q="What happened to his daughter?",a="His willful daughter, Catelyn, ran off to Booty Bay to become a pirate, and she is known there as Catelyn the Blade. Ansirem had given her an ancient troll dagger he found while researching in Stranglethorn, and she took it with her.",al={"ansirem daughter","catelyn the blade","catelyn runeweaver"}},{q="What is his role in Dalaran?",a="Ansirem serves as a key Kirin Tor presence in the Violet Citadel, coordinating research, magical defense, and communication with allies while the city is rebuilt after the destruction wrought during the Third War.",al={"why is ansirem in alterac","ansirem dalaran","what is he doing here"}},{q="Did Ansirem fight in the Third War?",a="Yes. Ansirem has helped defend Dalaran for decades, and he lived through the Scourge's siege of the city, when Arthas guarded Kel'Thuzad's summoning of Archimonde. He survived its destruction and now helps rebuild it.",al={"ansirem scourge","did ansirem fight arthas"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="Ansirem is a revered member of the Council of Six, making him an enduring authority on disciplined arcane study.",["faction:Alliance"]="As a Kirin Tor leader based in Lordaeron, Ansirem remains aligned with Alliance interests as human spellcasters struggle to reclaim their lands from Scourge remnants."},kw={"ansirem","booty bay","catelyn","council of six","dalaran","violet citadel","kirin tor","revilgaz","runeweaver"},rel={"subzone:dalaran","zone:alterac","subzone:booty-bay","npc:baron-revilgaz","topic:third-war","topic:arthas-menethil","topic:alliance"},src={"Archmage Ansirem Runeweaver"}}
E["npc:bath-rah-the-windwatcher"] = {t="npc",n="Bath'rah the Windwatcher",z="alterac",s="Bath'rah the Windwatcher is a solitary jungle troll shaman and weaponcrafter dwelling amidst the ruins near Chillwind Point. Far from his tropical homelands, he studies the tempestuous elements of the northern mountains, seeking champions powerful enough to help him craft formidable weapons of wind.",h="Bath'rah the Windwatcher is a solitary jungle troll shaman and weaponcrafter dwelling amidst the ruins near...",sec={{t="Hermit of the Peaks",b="While most jungle trolls keep to the warm forests and coasts of the south, Bath'rah has embraced the solitary life of a mountain hermit among the cold ruins of the Alterac Mountains. A seasoned shaman and craftsman, he devotes his days to listening to the howling winds and communing with nature spirits. His obsession is not merely philosophical; he seeks to bind the fury of violent elemental storms into tangible armaments for those who possess the strength to wield them.",sp=0},{t="Master of Cyclonian",b="Bath'rah's greatest ambition revolves around Cyclonian, a monstrous wind elemental dwelling within the surrounding peaks. Unable to best such an entity alone, the Windwatcher enlists seasoned warriors and shamans to gather exotic elemental essences and call forth the beast. By slaying Cyclonian and claiming its elemental heart, Bath'rah harnesses raw tempests into legendary weapons renowned across Azeroth.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Bath'rah the Windwatcher?",a="Bath'rah is an eccentric jungle troll shaman and weaponcrafter living in seclusion among the ruins of the Alterac Mountains near Chillwind Point. He helps seasoned adventurers harness elemental powers into mighty weapons.",al={"bathrah identity","who is bathrah","windwatcher lore"},it="identity"},{q="Why is a jungle troll living in Alterac?",a="Bath'rah lives as a hermit near Chillwind Point, studying elemental power and helping capable adventurers forge weapons. His reasons for leaving his former homeland are not established.",al={"why is bathrah in alterac","troll in alterac mountains"},it="why_here"},{q="What is Cyclonian?",a="Cyclonian is a massive, violent wind elemental haunting the ruins around Bath'rah's sanctuary. Bath'rah requires the creature's core to forge weapons infused with elemental wind.",al={"who is cyclonian","what does bathrah summon"},it="target"},{q="Why do warriors seek him out?",a="Warriors travel from all across the world to Bath'rah because he knows how to forge the iconic Whirlwind weapons. Defeating Cyclonian under his guidance yields arms infused with howling gales.",al={"bathrah warrior quest","whirlwind axe guy"},it="purpose"},{q="Does Bath'rah only help members of the Horde?",a="Bath'rah lives apart from major faction politics as a solitary hermit. He is primarily focused on elemental craftsmanship and will assist capable warriors and shamans who respect the spirits and aid his elemental work.",al={"is bathrah hostile","bathrah alliance"},it="side"},{q="What does Bath'rah the Windwatcher want?",a="Bath'rah seeks a worthy champion capable of confronting and defeating Cyclonian, a raging elemental residing near his camp. He covets the creature's heart, hoping to harness its raw primordial energy to forge an extraordinary weapon of immense power.",al={"bath'rah wants","what does bathrah want","bathrah goal"},it="wants",add="4f68ea16"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="Bath'rah is famous among veteran fighters for guiding them through the trials necessary to forge iconic Whirlwind armaments using the essence of the elemental Cyclonian.",["class:Shaman"]="As a fellow master of the elements, Bath'rah shares a deep spiritual connection with shamans pursuing deeper communion with the spirits of earth, water, and air."},kw={"alterac","bath'rah","chillwind","cyclonian","elemental","shaman","whirlwind","windwatcher"},rel={"subzone:chillwind-point","zone:alterac","quest:1791","topic:troll"},src={"Bath'rah the Windwatcher"}}
E["npc:lieutenant-haggerdin"] = {t="npc",n="Lieutenant Haggerdin",z="alterac",s="Lieutenant Haggerdin is a dwarven officer stationed upon the Headland in the Alterac Mountains. Standing watch outside the fortified gate to Alterac Valley, he acts as the primary recruitment and liaison officer for the Stormpike Guard. He evaluates aspiring Alliance champions and rewards those who prove their valor against the Frostwolf Clan.",h="Lieutenant Haggerdin is a dwarven officer stationed upon the Headland in the Alterac Mountains.",sec={{t="Gatekeeper of the Headland",b="Perched in the snowy heights of the Headland above the Hillsbrad Foothills, Lieutenant Haggerdin oversees the muster point for the Alliance's ongoing campaign in Alterac Valley. Dwarven banners flutter beside the massive wooden gate as recruits and veterans assemble under his watchful eye, preparing to plunge into the frigid warzone.",sp=0},{t="Voice of the Stormpike Guard",b="Serving the Stormpike Expedition, Haggerdin ensures that only tested warriors represent Ironforge and the Grand Alliance in the valley. Through challenges like the Proving Grounds, he tasks recruits with recovering banners and relics, and bestows official commendations, insignias, and rank recognitions as soldiers rise through the ranks of the Stormpike Guard.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Lieutenant Haggerdin?",a="Lieutenant Haggerdin is a dwarf officer representing the Stormpike Guard. Stationed at the entrance to Alterac Valley on the Headland in the Alterac Mountains, he oversees Alliance recruitment and rewards battlefield honors.",al={"haggerdin","who is haggerdin","lieutenant haggerdin alterac"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Lieutenant Haggerdin?",a="He is located in the northern Alterac Mountains on the Headland, standing just outside the portal and gates leading directly into Alterac Valley.",al={"haggerdin location","where is lieutenant haggerdin","alterac valley entrance alliance"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What role does Haggerdin play in the Stormpike Guard?",a="He serves as a field liaison and quartermaster officer, administering recruitment trials such as the Proving Grounds and rewarding Alliance fighters with higher ranks and insignia as their reputation with the Stormpike Guard grows.",al={"what does haggerdin do","haggerdin quests","stormpike guard officer"},it="purpose"},{q="Why is the Alliance fighting in Alterac Valley?",a="The Stormpike Expedition journeyed into the valley to excavate ancient relics and dwarven history, but their arrival sparked a fierce territorial conflict with the resident Frostwolf orcs and their Horde allies.",al={"why alterac valley","stormpike expedition goal","alterac conflict"},it="conflict"},{q="Can Horde players interact with Lieutenant Haggerdin?",a="No. Lieutenant Haggerdin is an active Alliance officer and will attack any Horde champions who venture near the Headland gate.",al={"is haggerdin hostile to horde","horde haggerdin","can horde talk to haggerdin"},it="hostile",gp=true},{q="What is the Proving Grounds trial?",a="The Proving Grounds is an introductory assignment Haggerdin gives to prospective Alliance soldiers to verify their competence and resolve before committing fully to the Alterac Valley war effort.",al={"proving grounds quest","proving grounds alterac","haggerdin proving grounds"}},{q="Whose side is Lieutenant Haggerdin on?",a="Lieutenant Haggerdin is thoroughly loyal to the Alliance, serving specifically within the Stormpike Guard. Operating at the northern edge of the foothills near Alterac Valley, he acts as an officer and muster agent for Alliance forces rallying against the Frostwolf orcs.",al={"haggerdin faction","is haggerdin alliance","haggerdin allegiance"},it="side",add="1d45d886"},{q="What does Lieutenant Haggerdin want?",a="Haggerdin wants capable Alliance champions to bolster the Stormpike Guard's ranks in Alterac Valley. He tests new recruits to ensure they can survive the freezing wilderness, recognizes seasoned veterans with ranks and insignias as their deeds grow, and seeks the downfall of threats like the Winterax troll champion, Korrak.",al={"what does haggerdin want","haggerdin goals","haggerdin purpose"},it="wants",add="5fb68a23"},{q="Why is Lieutenant Haggerdin here in the Alterac foothills?",a="Lieutenant Haggerdin is stationed at the Headland overlooking the gate to Alterac Valley to organize and vet incoming Alliance forces. Because the ongoing clash between the Stormpike Expedition and the Frostwolf Clan demands constant reinforcement, he stands guard at the staging grounds to recruit and honor those willing to fight in the snow.",al={"why is haggerdin here","why is haggerdin in alterac","haggerdin post"},it="why_here",add="96f37aaa"},{q="Who is Lieutenant Haggerdin tied to?",a="Haggerdin is tied directly to the Stormpike Guard, the military arm of Ironforge's Stormpike Expedition led by General Vanndar Stormpike. He serves as an officer linking Alliance recruits arriving through the Alterac Mountains to the regiment fighting deep within Alterac Valley.",al={"haggerdin ties","haggerdin stormpike guard","who does haggerdin serve"},it="ties",add="9b7a183a"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Lieutenant Haggerdin is your primary contact outside Alterac Valley, offering the credentials and official honors earned while clashing with the Frostwolf Clan.",["race:Dwarf"]="A proud officer of the Stormpike clan, Haggerdin embodies Ironforge's resolute determination to uncover their titan heritage in the snowy crags of Alterac.",["faction:Horde"]="A stalwart sentinel guarding the Alliance portal into Alterac Valley, Haggerdin directs the reinforcements sent to crush the Frostwolf orcs."},kw={"alterac","dwarf","frostwolf","haggerdin","headland","ironforge","lieutenant","proving grounds","stormpike"},rel={"zone:alterac","topic:dwarf","topic:alliance","topic:horde","zone:hillsbrad","topic:alterac-kingdom"},src={"Lieutenant Haggerdin"}}
E["npc:lord-jorach-ravenholdt"] = {t="npc",n="Lord Jorach Ravenholdt",z="alterac",s="Lord Jorach Ravenholdt is the master of Ravenholdt, an elite guild of rogues and assassins operating out of a secluded estate in the Alterac Mountains. He directs the league's clandestine operations, training promising operatives while waging a bitter war against the regional bandits of the Syndicate.",h="Lord Jorach Ravenholdt is the master of Ravenholdt, an elite guild of rogues and assassins operating out of a...",sec={{t="Master of the Assassin's League",b="Lord Jorach Ravenholdt presides over the Assassin's League from his hidden manor nestled in the crags between Alterac and Hillsbrad. A nobleman of mysterious heritage, he opens his halls to outlaws, cutpurses, and assassins regardless of allegiance, provided they exhibit exceptional skill and respect his authority. Under his command, the league acts as both a fraternity for master thieves and an independent syndicate for wetwork and espionage. Ravenholdt harbors a fierce hatred for the Syndicate—the band of disgraced Alterac nobles turned outlaws—and routinely directs his subordinates and visiting freelancers to sabotage their camps and plunder their assets.",sp=0},{t="Secrets in the Shadows",b="While ostensibly preoccupied with local skirmishes, Lord Ravenholdt directs far-reaching operations across Azeroth. Rogues who prove their loyalty are enlisted in intricate, continent-spanning tasks to retrieve guarded artifacts. Among these was the recovery of a mysterious Sealed Azure Bag, stolen from him and ferried to furbolgs in Azshara, which required the arcane decoding of Archmage Xylem and an Azure Key wrested from the Sunken Temple. Ravenholdt also coordinates the development of lethal new compounds, dispatching his scouts to gather lethal venom from ancient horrors across the realm.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Lord Jorach Ravenholdt?",a="He is the aristocratic leader of the Assassin's League, a covert society of rogues headquartered at Ravenholdt Manor in the mountains above Hillsbrad Foothills. He trains master stealth operatives and coordinates discrete assassinations and intelligence gathering.",al={"who is jorach","ravenholdt leader","jorach lore"}},{q="Why does Ravenholdt hate the Syndicate?",a="Ravenholdt's estate sits directly within territory contested by the Syndicate, a network of former Alterac nobles turned ruthless outlaws. He views their crude banditry as an infection across the highlands and uses his guild's assassins to actively purge their strongholds.",al={"why syndicate enemy","ravenholdt vs syndicate","syndicate rivalry"}},{q="Is Lord Ravenholdt affiliated with the Alliance or Horde?",a="Ravenholdt operates strictly as an independent organization. Lord Jorach accepts rogues of both the Alliance and the Horde into his manor, caring only for professional prowess, stealth discipline, and absolute discretion rather than racial politics.",al={"is ravenholdt alliance","is jorach horde","ravenholdt faction"}},{q="What is inside the Sealed Azure Bag Jorach seeks?",a="The contents remain an intensely guarded secret. When presented with the Azure Key to finally unlock the enchanted satchel, Lord Jorach was bathed in an eerie golden light, staring inside with astonishment before swiftly stowing it away.",al={"sealed azure bag contents","azure bag mystery","what did jorach get"},sp=1}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="Lord Ravenholdt is the preeminent patron of master rogues across Azeroth, offering elite training, poisons, and prestigious contracts to those who earn his trust."},kw={"alterac","assassin's league","azure key","jorach","ravenholdt","rogue","syndicate","xylem"},rel={"subzone:ravenholdt-manor","topic:ravenholdt","topic:syndicate","zone:alterac","npc:archmage-xylem","subzone:temple-of-atal-hakkar","quest:2300","npc:mathias-shaw"},src={"Lord Jorach Ravenholdt"}}
E["quest:500"] = {t="quest",n="Crushridge Bounty",z="alterac",s="Marshal Redpath in Southshore warns that Crushridge ogres have settled by the ruins of Alterac and claimed them. A bounty is offered to anyone who will go north into the Alterac Mountains and hunt them.",h="Marshal Redpath in Southshore warns that Crushridge ogres have settled by the ruins of Alterac and claimed...",sec={{t="Ogres at the Door",b="Redpath's scouts report that the Crushridge ogres have dug a mound in the Alterac Mountains, close to the ruined city, and have taken over its ruins as well. Redpath will not let them grow cozy: ogres who feel safe will move down into the foothills, right to Southshore's door. So Redpath sends you north to hunt the ogres and bring back the Dirty Knucklebones they carry, for a bounty.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Marshal Redpath want the Crushridge ogres hunted?",a="Redpath fears the ogres will feel safe in their mound and the ruins of Alterac, and then move down into the foothills, which would put them at Southshore's door.",al={"why kill crushridge ogres","redpath motive","ogre bounty reason"}},{q="Where are the Crushridge ogres?",a="North, in the Alterac Mountains, where they have built a mound close to the ruined city of Alterac. Redpath's scouts say they hold the ruins too.",al={"ogre location","crushridge ogres where","where to find knucklebones"}},{q="What does Marshal Redpath want brought back?",a="Nine Dirty Knucklebones, which the Crushridge ogres carry, to be brought to Redpath in Southshore.",al={"what do i bring redpath","ogre proof","dirty knucklebones"}}},kw={"alterac","bounty","crushridge","knucklebones","ogres","redpath","southshore"},rel={"quest:504","subzone:southshore","zone:alterac","topic:alterac-kingdom"},m={start="Marshal Redpath",["end"]="Marshal Redpath",level="36",faction="Alliance",id=500},src={"Crushridge Bounty"}}
E["quest:504"] = {t="quest",n="Crushridge Warmongers",z="alterac",s="Marshal Redpath of Southshore wants the Crushridge ogres hit harder than before. You are sent into the Ruins of Alterac to find the Crushridge Warmongers, so the brutes will stay away from the Alliance.",h="Marshal Redpath of Southshore wants the Crushridge ogres hit harder than before.",sec={{t="A Harder Lesson",b="After Crushridge Bounty, Marshal Redpath wants the ogres to feel it in earnest. Redpath sends you into the Ruins of Alterac to seek out the Crushridge Warmongers and cut down plenty of them. Redpath holds that nothing else will teach the brutes to stay clear of Alliance territory.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends you after the Crushridge Warmongers?",a="Marshal Redpath in Southshore.",al={"who gives crushridge warmongers","questgiver crushridge warmongers","marshal redpath quest"}},{q="Where are the Crushridge Warmongers?",a="In the Ruins of Alterac, up in the mountains.",al={"where are crushridge warmongers","warmonger location","crushridge warmongers spot"}},{q="Why does Marshal Redpath want the Warmongers cut down?",a="Redpath believes nothing else will teach the Crushridge ogres to stay away from Alliance lands.",al={"why kill warmongers","purpose of crushridge warmongers","redpath reason ogres"}},{q="What comes before this quest?",a="It follows Crushridge Bounty, Redpath's first call to hunt the Crushridge ogres.",al={"prerequisite for crushridge warmongers","previous quest warmongers","chain before crushridge warmongers"}}},kw={"alterac","crushridge","ogres","redpath","ruins","southshore","warmongers"},rel={"quest:500","subzone:ruins-of-alterac","subzone:southshore","zone:alterac","topic:alterac-kingdom","topic:alliance"},m={start="Marshal Redpath",["end"]="Marshal Redpath",level="40",faction="Alliance",id=504},src={"Crushridge Warmongers"}}
E["quest:505"] = {t="quest",n="Syndicate Assassins",z="alterac",s="Magistrate Henry Maleb, newly assigned to Southshore after the previous magistrate was assassinated, believes the Syndicate hired the killers. The trail led to a Syndicate camp north of Tarren Mill, and Maleb wants the members there slain.",h="Magistrate Henry Maleb, newly assigned to Southshore after the previous magistrate was assassinated, believes...",sec={{t="A Magistrate Murdered",b="Magistrate Henry Maleb is the new magistrate of Southshore, assigned after the previous magistrate was assassinated. The assassins were never found, yet Maleb is almost certain the Syndicate hired them. The Syndicate is a gang of thieves, run by villainous nobles from Alterac, a kingdom that has since fallen. Maleb's last clues pointed to a Syndicate camp north of Tarren Mill, which the Horde occupies, and Maleb asks you to slay the Syndicate members found there.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Magistrate Henry Maleb want the Syndicate slain?",a="The previous magistrate of Southshore was assassinated, and Maleb is almost certain the Syndicate hired the killers, who were never found.",al={"why kill syndicate","syndicate motive","who killed the magistrate"}},{q="Who leads the Syndicate?",a="Wicked nobles of the fallen kingdom of Alterac lead it, and its members are thieves.",al={"who runs the syndicate","syndicate leaders","syndicate alterac"}},{q="Where is the Syndicate camp?",a="North of Tarren Mill, which the Horde has occupied. Maleb's last clues led there.",al={"where are the syndicate footpads","syndicate camp location","where to find syndicate thieves"}}},kw={"alterac","footpad","henry maleb","magistrate","southshore","syndicate","tarren mill","thief"},rel={"npc:magistrate-henry-maleb","subzone:southshore","topic:syndicate","topic:alterac-kingdom","zone:alterac","subzone:tarren-mill"},m={start="Magistrate Henry Maleb",["end"]="Magistrate Henry Maleb",level="33",faction="Alliance",id=505},src={"Syndicate Assassins","In-game quest text: Syndicate Assassins"}}
E["quest:510"] = {t="quest",n="Foreboding Plans",z="alterac",s="The Syndicate documents hold a list of supplies the Syndicate asked for, wanted in a hurry for what the papers call an important undertaking against Southshore. Magistrate Henry Maleb in Southshore awaits them.",h="The Syndicate documents hold a list of supplies the Syndicate asked for, wanted in a hurry for what the...",sec={{t="The Supply List",b="The documents include a list of requested supplies. Some are mundane: food, weapons and clothing. Others are more exotic: masks, oil and poison. What stands out most is the urgency, for the papers say the supplies were needed soon, for an important undertaking against Southshore. Magistrate Henry Maleb in Southshore is the one to receive them.",sp=0},{t="Maleb's Verdict",b="Maleb reads the documents and finds them very troubling. From what they say, and from the Syndicate's past deeds, Maleb concludes that these cutthroats have gone to war against the town.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What do the Syndicate documents say?",a="They list requested supplies: ordinary things like food, weapons and clothing, and stranger ones like masks, oil and poison. The papers stress that these were needed soon for an important operation against Southshore.",al={"what are the foreboding plans","syndicate documents contents","what is in the plans"}},{q="Who should see these plans?",a="Magistrate Henry Maleb in Southshore.",al={"who do i bring the plans to","foreboding plans turn in","where do the plans go"}}},kw={"alterac mountains","foreboding plans","magistrate henry maleb","southshore","syndicate","syndicate documents"},rel={"quest:512","npc:magistrate-henry-maleb","subzone:southshore","topic:syndicate","zone:alterac"},m={start="Syndicate Documents",["end"]="Magistrate Henry Maleb",level="34",faction="Alliance",id=510},src={"Foreboding Plans (quest)"}}
E["quest:511"] = {t="quest",n="Encrypted Letter",z="alterac",s="Among the Syndicate documents, one of the letters on a table is encrypted and inscrutable. Loremaster Dibbs in Southshore is the one to show it to.",h="Among the Syndicate documents, one of the letters on a table is encrypted and inscrutable.",sec={{t="A Letter No One Can Read",b="Among the Syndicate documents lies a table of letters, and one of them is encrypted and inscrutable. Loremaster Dibbs in Southshore is the one to show it to.",sp=0},{t="What Dibbs Makes of It",b="Dibbs takes a closer look and admits never having seen this form of encryption before. Dibbs confesses that such learning is by no means complete.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where does the letter come from?",a="It is one of the letters on a table among the Syndicate documents, and this one is encrypted.",al={"letter origin","where find letter","encrypted letter start"}},{q="Who is the letter taken to?",a="Loremaster Dibbs in Southshore.",al={"who reads letter","who can decipher it","dibbs letter"}}},kw={"alterac","encrypted letter","hillsbrad foothills","loremaster dibbs","southshore","syndicate documents"},rel={"quest:514","subzone:southshore","zone:hillsbrad","zone:alterac"},m={start="Syndicate Documents",["end"]="Loremaster Dibbs",level="34",faction="Alliance",id=511},src={"Encrypted Letter (Hillsbrad Foothills)"}}
E["quest:512"] = {t="quest",n="Noble Deaths",z="alterac",s="Magistrate Henry Maleb fears that the Syndicate's leaders are bent on Southshore's ruin and wants them struck down before their plans come to pass. You are to head north into the Alterac Mountains, to Strahnbrad's ruins, which the Syndicate is thought to use as a headquarters.",h="Magistrate Henry Maleb fears that the Syndicate's leaders are bent on Southshore's ruin and wants them struck...",sec={{t="Hunting the Syndicate's Leaders",b="After Foreboding Plans, Magistrate Henry Maleb in Southshore wants the Syndicate's leadership dealt with before its plans are realized. The Syndicate's cutthroats answer to former Alterac nobles, who may be hiding as ordinary agents. A noble can be known by the signet ring worn. Maleb asks for seven Alterac signet rings to be brought back to him in Southshore, and he thinks the Syndicate has made a headquarters of Strahnbrad's ruins, up north in the Alterac Mountains.",sp=0},{t="Maleb's Hope",b="Maleb is convinced that a Syndicate without its nobility could no longer act with decision, and would be reduced to common thugs.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you to Strahnbrad?",a="Magistrate Henry Maleb in Southshore sends you north, to strike at the leaders behind the Syndicate.",al={"quest giver","who gives noble deaths","henry maleb quest"}},{q="Where are the Syndicate nobles located?",a="Maleb thinks the Syndicate has made a headquarters of Strahnbrad's ruins, up north in the Alterac Mountains.",al={"where to go","strahnbrad location","syndicate nobles location"}},{q="How can you tell the nobles apart from ordinary Syndicate members?",a="The nobles may hide as normal Syndicate agents, but each can be known by the signet ring worn.",al={"identifying nobles","who drops rings","how to tell nobles"}},{q="What comes before this in the chain?",a="It follows Foreboding Plans.",al={"prerequisite quest","previous quest","noble deaths prequest"}}},kw={"alterac mountains","alterac signet ring","henry maleb","noble deaths","southshore","strahnbrad","syndicate"},rel={"quest:510","npc:magistrate-henry-maleb","subzone:strahnbrad","subzone:southshore","topic:syndicate","zone:alterac","topic:alterac-kingdom"},m={start="Magistrate Henry Maleb",["end"]="Magistrate Henry Maleb",level="36",faction="Alliance",id=512},src={"Noble Deaths"}}
E["quest:514"] = {t="quest",n="Letter to Stormpike",z="alterac",s="Loremaster Dibbs in Southshore holds a cleverly encrypted letter, and he knows someone in Ironforge who might decrypt it. He sends you with the letter to Prospector Stormpike, in the Library of the Hall of Explorers.",h="Loremaster Dibbs in Southshore holds a cleverly encrypted letter, and he knows someone in Ironforge who might...",sec={{t="A Colleague in Ironforge",b="Prospector Stormpike is to be found in the Library, in the Hall of Explorers in Ironforge. Dibbs wants you to tell Stormpike that he sent you, and to show the letter. Dibbs reckons that if anyone north of Blackrock Spire can read it, Stormpike is the one.",sp=0},{t="Stormpike's Welcome",b="Stormpike asks how the old bookworm is doing when he hears Dibbs sent you. Then he declares that encryption is a specialty of his and begins to look the letter over.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you to Ironforge with the letter?",a="Loremaster Dibbs in Southshore sends you, hoping a colleague in Ironforge can decrypt the letter.",al={"who gave me this quest","quest giver","who starts letter to stormpike"}},{q="Where is Prospector Stormpike located?",a="Prospector Stormpike is in the Library inside the Hall of Explorers in Ironforge.",al={"stormpike location","where is stormpike","prospector stormpike library"}},{q="Why does Dibbs believe Stormpike can read the letter?",a="Dibbs says that if anyone north of Blackrock Spire can read it, it is Stormpike.",al={"why stormpike","why send to stormpike","stormpike encryption"}}},kw={"encrypted letter","hall of explorers","ironforge library","letter to stormpike","loremaster dibbs","prospector stormpike","southshore"},rel={"quest:511","quest:525","npc:prospector-stormpike","subzone:library-ironforge","subzone:hall-of-explorers","zone:ironforge","subzone:southshore","zone:alterac"},m={start="Loremaster Dibbs",["end"]="Prospector Stormpike",level="34",faction="Alliance",id=514},src={"Letter to Stormpike"}}
E["quest:522"] = {t="quest",n="Assassin's Contract",z="alterac",s="A Shadowy Assassin in Hillsbrad Foothills carries a contract that orders the killing of Magistrate Henry Maleb. Red wax seals it, pressed with a distinctive signet ring, and you are to bring it to Maleb in Southshore.",h="A Shadowy Assassin in Hillsbrad Foothills carries a contract that orders the killing of Magistrate Henry...",sec={{t="A Marked Magistrate",b="The paper orders the killing of Magistrate Henry Maleb. A seal of red wax closes it, pressed with a distinctive signet ring. A Shadowy Assassin in Hillsbrad Foothills carries it, and Maleb in Southshore is the one to show it to.",sp=0},{t="Maleb's Verdict",b="Maleb looks over the contract and says it accounts for the recent attack on Southshore. Maleb is certain the Syndicate is after the magistrate's life, as it was after the previous magistrate's.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is written in the contract?",a="It orders the killing of Magistrate Henry Maleb, and red wax seals it, pressed with a distinctive signet ring.",al={"what does the contract say","assassins contract details","who is the target"}},{q="Where does this contract originate?",a="It is carried by a Shadowy Assassin in Hillsbrad Foothills.",al={"who dropped the contract","where to find contract","shadowy assassin drop"}},{q="To whom should the contract be delivered?",a="To Magistrate Henry Maleb in Southshore, the magistrate the contract marks for death.",al={"who do I give the contract to","where to turn in assassins contract","maleb location"}}},kw={"assassin's contract","hillsbrad foothills","magistrate henry maleb","shadowy assassin","signet ring","southshore","syndicate"},rel={"npc:magistrate-henry-maleb","quest:523","subzone:southshore","zone:hillsbrad","topic:syndicate","zone:alterac"},m={start="Assassin's Contract",["end"]="Magistrate Henry Maleb",level="38",faction="Alliance",id=522},src={"Assassin's Contract (quest)"}}
E["quest:523"] = {t="quest",n="Baron's Demise",z="alterac",s="The contract you recovered bears the name of Baron Vardus, a nobleman from the old kingdom of Alterac. Magistrate Henry Maleb in Southshore wants him found and brought to justice, and asks for the baron's head.",h="The contract you recovered bears the name of Baron Vardus, a nobleman from the old kingdom of Alterac.",sec={{t="Justice for a Contract",b="After Assassin's Contract, Magistrate Henry Maleb tells you that Baron Vardus put his name to the contract. Vardus is a nobleman from the old kingdom of Alterac, a man of cold heart and brutal ways, so Maleb is not surprised to find him behind it. Southshore will not let the baron send his thugs against the town without answering for it. Maleb wants him found among the Syndicate's haunts, perhaps in Strahnbrad's ruins or in the valley north of them, and asks for the baron's head.",sp=0},{t="Maleb's Relief",b="When you bring the baron's head, Maleb thanks you and says that knowing the villain has lost his own lets the magistrate rest a little easier.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Baron Vardus?",a="A nobleman from the old kingdom of Alterac, with a cold heart and brutal ways. His name is on the contract that marked Maleb for death.",al={"baron vardus lore","who is vardus","vardus alterac"}},{q="Why does Magistrate Maleb want Baron Vardus dead?",a="Vardus put his name to the contract you recovered, and Maleb will not let him send thugs against Southshore without answering for it.",al={"why kill baron vardus","maleb vardus","reason for baron's demise"}},{q="Where can Baron Vardus be found?",a="Maleb thinks Vardus is somewhere in the Syndicate's haunts, perhaps in Strahnbrad's ruins or in the valley north of them.",al={"baron vardus location","where is vardus","strahnbrad vardus"}},{q="What comes before this?",a="It follows Assassin's Contract, the contract you recovered that bears the baron's signature.",al={"baron's demise prequest","chain before baron's demise","assassin's contract prerequisite"}}},kw={"alterac mountains","baron vardus","baron's demise","magistrate henry maleb","southshore","strahnbrad","syndicate"},rel={"quest:522","npc:magistrate-henry-maleb","subzone:southshore","subzone:strahnbrad","topic:syndicate","topic:alterac-kingdom","zone:alterac"},m={start="Magistrate Henry Maleb",["end"]="Magistrate Henry Maleb",level="40",faction="Alliance",id=523},src={"Baron's Demise"}}
E["quest:525"] = {t="quest",n="Further Mysteries",z="alterac",s="Prospector Stormpike has decrypted the letter you found among thieves in the Alterac foothills, but cannot make sense of it. He tells you to take it to the magistrate of Southshore.",h="Prospector Stormpike has decrypted the letter you found among thieves in the Alterac foothills, but cannot...",sec={{t="A Letter Without Meaning",b="After Letter to Stormpike, the prospector says he has decrypted the letter but cannot tell what it means. He finds it very strange that you came by it among thieves in the Alterac foothills. The letter is cryptic, yet Southshore lies nearest to Alterac, so if a threat is brewing, the magistrate there should hear of it. You are to carry the decrypted letter to Magistrate Henry Maleb.",sp=0},{t="What Maleb Reads",b="Maleb studies the letter and judges that no thief and no Alterac noble could have written it. To Maleb it points to a darker power behind the Syndicate, and Maleb shudders to think what that power might be.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you with the decrypted letter?",a="Prospector Stormpike, who decrypted it but cannot make sense of it, tells you to take it to the magistrate of Southshore.",al={"who gives further mysteries","further mysteries questgiver","where does further mysteries start"}},{q="Who needs to see the decrypted letter?",a="Magistrate Henry Maleb in Southshore. Stormpike points out that Southshore lies nearest to Alterac, so if a threat is brewing, the magistrate should know.",al={"who gets the decrypted letter","further mysteries turn in","where do i take the letter"}},{q="Where did the original encrypted letter come from?",a="You found it among thieves in the Alterac foothills before it went to Prospector Stormpike.",al={"origin of the decrypted letter","where was letter found","who had the letter"}}},kw={"alterac","decrypted letter","further mysteries","magistrate henry maleb","prospector stormpike","southshore","syndicate"},rel={"quest:514","quest:537","npc:prospector-stormpike","npc:magistrate-henry-maleb","subzone:southshore","topic:syndicate","zone:alterac"},m={start="Prospector Stormpike",["end"]="Magistrate Henry Maleb",level="34",faction="Alliance",id=525},src={"Further Mysteries"}}
E["quest:535"] = {t="quest",n="Valik",z="alterac",s="Henchman Valik lies injured and dying in a Syndicate camp, confronted by an enemy. Certain you will kill them anyway, Valik strikes a bargain: a mug of Southshore Stout in exchange for answers.",h="Henchman Valik lies injured and dying in a Syndicate camp, confronted by an enemy.",sec={{t="A Dying Bargain",b="Valik is injured and dying, and finds you standing before them as an enemy. Valik expects you to kill them regardless, but offers a bargain: carry a mug of Southshore Stout to the Syndicate camp, and Valik will answer your questions. Valik even wonders aloud whether your kind drinks at all.",sp=0},{t="Valik's Last Drink",b="Valik declares the stout the sweetest thing ever tasted, given the death waiting. Valik hands over something of no use to the dead, then tells you to get on with it.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Valik?",a="Henchman Valik is an injured and dying henchman of the Syndicate, found in the Syndicate camp.",al={"henchman valik","who is valik","valik alterac"}},{q="What does Valik want?",a="A mug of Southshore Stout, brought to the Syndicate camp.",al={"what does valik need","valik drink","valik stout"}},{q="What does Valik promise in return for the stout?",a="Valik promises to share what you are after, though expecting to be killed afterward anyway.",al={"valik reward lore","what does valik tell you","valik trade"}}},kw={"alterac mountains","henchman valik","southshore stout","syndicate","valik"},rel={"subzone:southshore","topic:syndicate","zone:alterac"},m={start="Henchman Valik",["end"]="Henchman Valik",level="34",faction="Horde",id=535},src={"Valik (quest)"}}
E["quest:537"] = {t="quest",n="Dark Council",z="alterac",s="Magistrate Henry Maleb in Southshore has learned that the letter you brought came from a being who goes by Nagaz and belongs to the Argus Wake. If the Argus Wake is allied with the Syndicate, Maleb says, they must be a threat. You are sent to hunt down Nagaz and the Argus Shadow Mages in the Uplands.",h="Magistrate Henry Maleb in Southshore has learned that the letter you brought came from a being who goes by...",sec={{t="Envoys in the Uplands",b="After Further Mysteries, Maleb tells you the letter came from a being who goes by Nagaz and belongs to the Argus Wake. Maleb does not know what the Argus Wake is, but an alliance with the Syndicate would make them a threat. Maleb wants Nagaz and the Argus Shadow Mages named in the letter found and killed, and asks for the head of Nagaz. You are to search the Uplands, north of Strahnbrad, where the Syndicate is strongest. Maleb hopes the Argus Wake's envoys are there.",sp=0},{t="What Maleb Concludes",b="Maleb finds it unwelcome that a group like the Argus Wake might run the Syndicate. Nagaz was only another's servant, Maleb adds, and the Argus Wake's reach may go deep across the continent, or even the whole world.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you after Nagaz?",a="Magistrate Henry Maleb in Southshore, who read the letter you brought him.",al={"who gives dark council","dark council questgiver","where to pick up dark council"}},{q="Where are Nagaz and the Argus Shadow Mages located?",a="Maleb tells you to search the Uplands, north of Strahnbrad, where the Syndicate is strongest.",al={"where is nagaz","argus shadow mage location","where are the uplands"}},{q="What is the Argus Wake?",a="Maleb does not know. He only knows that Nagaz belongs to it and that, if it is allied with the Syndicate, it must be a threat.",al={"who are argus wake","what is argus wake","argus wake lore"}},{q="What happens before this?",a="It follows Further Mysteries, in which you brought the decrypted letter to Maleb.",al={"prereq for dark council","previous quest","what quest comes before"}}},kw={"argus shadow mage","argus wake","dark council","henry maleb","nagaz","southshore","strahnbrad","syndicate","uplands"},rel={"npc:magistrate-henry-maleb","quest:525","subzone:uplands","subzone:strahnbrad","subzone:southshore","zone:alterac","topic:syndicate"},m={start="Magistrate Henry Maleb",["end"]="Magistrate Henry Maleb",level="40",faction="Alliance",id=537},src={"Dark Council"}}
E["quest:551"] = {t="quest",n="The Ensorcelled Parchment",z="alterac",s="A spell on a parchment makes its writing unreadable, apart from one word at the top: Nagaz. You are to take it to Loremaster Dibbs in Southshore.",h="A spell on a parchment makes its writing unreadable, apart from one word at the top: Nagaz.",sec={{t="A Spell-Veiled Parchment",b="A spell lies on the parchment and keeps its writing from being deciphered. Only a single word at the top can be made out, the name Nagaz. You are to take it to Loremaster Dibbs in Southshore.",sp=0},{t="What Dibbs Makes of It",b="Dibbs asks whether this is yet more encrypted notes. Dibbs wishes every odd scrap of writing drifting out of Alterac could be decoded, but admits to lacking the knowledge.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is written on the parchment?",a="A spell keeps the writing from being read, save for a single word at the top: Nagaz.",al={"what does the ensorcelled parchment say","parchment text","ensorcelled parchment words"}},{q="Who should see the parchment?",a="Loremaster Dibbs in Southshore, who takes in scraps of lore gathered from the mountains.",al={"loremaster dibbs","who is dibbs","southshore loremaster"}}},kw={"alterac","dibbs","ensorcelled","nagaz","parchment","southshore"},rel={"quest:554","subzone:southshore","zone:alterac","topic:alterac-kingdom"},m={start="Ensorcelled Parchment",["end"]="Loremaster Dibbs",level="40",faction="Alliance",id=551},src={"The Ensorcelled Parchment"}}
E["quest:554"] = {t="quest",n="Stormpike's Deciphering",z="alterac",s="Loremaster Dibbs sends you to Ironforge with the ensorcelled parchment, hoping Prospector Stormpike, a master of decryption and deciphering, can make sense of it.",h="Loremaster Dibbs sends you to Ironforge with the ensorcelled parchment, hoping Prospector Stormpike, a master...",sec={{t="A Master of Decryption",b="After The Ensorcelled Parchment, Dibbs tells you to take it to Prospector Stormpike, who is at his studies in Ironforge's Prospector headquarters. Dibbs says to mention that he sent you, since he has been sending Stormpike quite a lot of business lately.",sp=0},{t="A Matter of Time",b="Stormpike finds the parchment covered in a very intricate, finely woven spell. He says he can untangle it, but it will take time, and time is valuable to him, so he offers to buy it from you. Once you agree, he says he believes no scholar but himself has the skill to translate it, and promises to send for you if its contents prove interesting.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you to Prospector Stormpike?",a="Loremaster Dibbs, who calls Stormpike a master of decryption and deciphering.",al={"who gives the quest","quest giver","loremaster dibbs quest"}},{q="Where can Prospector Stormpike be found?",a="He is at his studies in Ironforge's Prospector headquarters.",al={"stormpike location","where is stormpike","prospector headquarters"}},{q="Why is the parchment difficult to read?",a="A spell lies on it and keeps the writing from being deciphered, and only the name Nagaz can be read at the top.",al={"why ensorcelled parchment","parchment spell","why decipher"}},{q="What comes before this step?",a="It follows The Ensorcelled Parchment, which brought the enchanted parchment to Dibbs.",al={"previous quest","chain start","prerequisite"}}},kw={"deciphering","dibbs","ensorcelled parchment","ironforge","prospector headquarters","stormpike"},rel={"npc:prospector-stormpike","quest:551","zone:ironforge","zone:alterac"},m={start="Loremaster Dibbs",["end"]="Prospector Stormpike",level="40",faction="Alliance",id=554},src={"Stormpike's Deciphering"}}
E["quest:92432"] = {t="quest",n="An Alarming Request",z="alterac",s="Emissary Jacques in Southshore brings bad news out of Dalaran: the city's ley lines have been thrown off, and its constructs have turned erratic and destructive. Archmage Modera sent Jacques to find outside aid, and you are told to seek her image near Dalaran, beside Lordamere Lake.",h="Emissary Jacques in Southshore brings bad news out of Dalaran: the city's ley lines have been thrown off, and...",sec={{t="Trouble in Dalaran",b="Emissary Jacques says Dalaran's ley lines have been disrupted, and the city's constructs now behave erratically and destructively. The cause is not yet known. The high council has ordered the matter kept private so as not to bring shame to the order, but Jacques says the charade cannot go on forever, for the city is being overrun. Archmage Modera sent Jacques to seek outside aid, and you are to find her image near Dalaran, beside Lordamere Lake.",sp=0},{t="Modera's Welcome",b="At her image, Modera notes that Jacques was successful in finding aid. Though it is not strictly permitted, she says pride should not turn allies away in the city's desperate hour. She warns that things are anything but under control, whatever the guards would have you believe.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Emissary Jacques?",a="Jacques is an emissary of Dalaran in Southshore, sent by Archmage Modera to seek outside aid.",al={"emissary jacques","who is jacques","who gives an alarming request"}},{q="What is happening in Dalaran?",a="The city's ley lines have been disrupted, and its constructs now behave erratically and destructively. The cause is not yet known, and the city is being overrun.",al={"what is wrong in dalaran","dalaran problem","why are constructs attacking dalaran"}},{q="Why is the matter being kept private?",a="The high council ordered the trouble kept private so as not to bring shame to the order.",al={"why secrecy dalaran","why hide the constructs","dalaran high council secret"}},{q="Where is the Image of Archmage Modera located?",a="Near Dalaran, beside Lordamere Lake.",al={"where to find modera","modera location","image of archmage modera"}}},kw={"alterac","constructs","dalaran","jacques","ley lines","lordamere","modera","southshore"},rel={"subzone:dalaran","subzone:southshore","subzone:lordamere-lake","zone:alterac"},m={start="Emissary Jacques",["end"]="Image of Archmage Modera",level="33",faction="Alliance",id=92432},src={"An Alarming Request"},fv=true}
E["quest:92434"] = {t="quest",n="Blood in the Streets",z="alterac",s="Dalaran's barrier has come down, and turmoil grips the city. With its patrols dealt with, Magus Wordeen Voidglare says there is no better time to slip inside and learn the mages' secrets. You are to carry the key from the internment camp to the city's sewers on its northern edge.",h="Dalaran's barrier has come down, and turmoil grips the city.",sec={{t="A Disagreeable Way In",b="After Dalaran Patrols, Magus Wordeen Voidglare says that whatever lowered Dalaran's barrier has thrown the city into turmoil, so now is the time for the Horde to get inside and learn the mages' secrets. You are to take the key from the internment camp and look for the sewers on the city's northern edge, by Lordamere Lake. With luck, the mages saw no need to ward so disagreeable an entrance.",sp=0},{t="What Comes of the Key",b="The Image of Archmage Modera tells you to stay your weapon. She says the key will not be enough to get past her wards, since the mages would not leave such a weakness open at a time like this. She says the Horde's interest in her city is no coincidence, that she was counting on it, and that she has a proposition for you.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you into Dalaran's sewers?",a="Magus Wordeen Voidglare, after the patrols have been dealt with.",al={"blood in the streets quest giver","who gives blood in the streets","wordeen voidglare quest"}},{q="Where is the entrance into Dalaran located?",a="Wordeen points you to the sewers on the northern edge of the city, by Lordamere Lake.",al={"where are dalaran sewers","sewer entrance lordamere lake","how to enter dalaran"}},{q="What key is used to attempt entry?",a="The grimy key from the internment camp.",al={"grimy key dalaran","where did the key come from","internment camp key"}},{q="Why is Dalaran vulnerable right now?",a="Its barrier has come down, and turmoil grips the city.",al={"why is dalaran barrier down","what happened to dalaran shield"}}},kw={"alterac","blood in the streets","dalaran","grimy key","lordamere lake","modera","sewers","wordeen voidglare"},rel={"quest:545","subzone:dalaran","subzone:sewers","subzone:lordamere-lake","topic:horde","zone:alterac"},m={start="Magus Wordeen Voidglare",["end"]="Image of Archmage Modera",level="34",faction="Horde",id=92434},src={"Blood in the Streets"},fv=true}
E["quest:92459"] = {t="quest",n="Friend of the Kirin Tor",z="alterac",s="Archmage Modera's image admits that the council will dislike hearing of the subterfuge, yet cannot argue with results: Dalaran is calming, and the wards may come down. She gives you an arcane mote to take to Archmage Celindra, in the Violet Citadel.",h="Archmage Modera's image admits that the council will dislike hearing of the subterfuge, yet cannot argue with...",sec={{t="The Good Word",b="The Image of Archmage Modera admits that the council will dislike hearing of the subterfuge, yet cannot argue with results. The city is calming, and the wards may now be lowered. She thinks you should be the one to carry the good word, and gives you an arcane mote to take to Archmage Celindra, in Dalaran's Violet Citadel.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends you to Archmage Celindra?",a="The Image of Archmage Modera, who has you deliver the good word about Dalaran.",al={"who gives friend of the kirin tor","friend of the kirin tor quest giver","modera quest"}},{q="Where is Archmage Celindra?",a="In the Violet Citadel, in the City of Dalaran.",al={"where to turn in friend of the kirin tor","who is celindra","archmage celindra location"}},{q="What item do you carry to the Violet Citadel?",a="An arcane mote, which Modera gives you to take to Archmage Celindra.",al={"friend of the kirin tor item","what is the arcane mote"}},{q="What is the good word?",a="That Dalaran is calming down and its wards are free to be lowered.",al={"what news does modera send","why lower the wards"}}},kw={"alterac","arcane mote","celindra","dalaran","kirin tor","modera","violet citadel","wards"},rel={"subzone:dalaran","zone:alterac"},m={start="Image of Archmage Modera",["end"]="Archmage Celindra",level="33",faction="Alliance",id=92459},src={"Friend of the Kirin Tor"},fv=true}
E["quest:93680"] = {t="quest",n="Key to the City",z="alterac",s="Magus Wordeen Voidglare in Tarren Mill wants to know more about the Kirin Tor, whose city Archimonde destroyed and who have now rebuilt Dalaran on the Dark Lady's very doorstep. You are to search the Kirin Tor camps for something that can get the Horde into the city unnoticed.",h="Magus Wordeen Voidglare in Tarren Mill wants to know more about the Kirin Tor, whose city Archimonde...",sec={{t="The Rebuilt City",b="The Alliance once had an army of mages, the Kirin Tor, but the demonic Burning Legion proved the stronger. In a single stroke the arch demon Archimonde levelled their city, and the survivors were left as dispossessed vagabonds. Now they have rebuilt Dalaran, on the Dark Lady's very doorstep. Magus Wordeen Voidglare in Tarren Mill wants to know more, and sends you to search their camps for something, such as an ancient tome or a secret relic, that can get the Horde into the city unnoticed. What you bring back is a grimy Dalaran sewer key.",sp=0},{t="Wordeen's Answer",b="On seeing a sewer key, Wordeen says that thankfully someone else will be the one using it. There is work to do before it is safe to use.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who gives the request for Key to the City?",a="Magus Wordeen Voidglare, in Tarren Mill.",al={"who gives key to the city","key to the city questgiver","where do i start key to the city"}},{q="Why is the Horde interested in Dalaran?",a="The Kirin Tor, whose city Archimonde destroyed, have rebuilt Dalaran on the Dark Lady's very doorstep. Wordeen wants to know more and needs a way in unnoticed.",al={"why dalaran","why watch dalaran","what are the mages doing"}},{q="What item are you sent to find?",a="A Dalaran sewer key, a grimy key, to be found in the Kirin Tor camps.",al={"what do i get for wordeen","what is the key","key to the city item"}}},kw={"archimonde","burning legion","dalaran","grimy key","kirin tor","sewer key","tarren mill","wordeen voidglare"},rel={"subzone:tarren-mill","subzone:dalaran","quest:545","zone:alterac","topic:burning-legion"},m={start="Magus Wordeen Voidglare",level="33",faction="Horde",id=93680},src={"Key to the City (Forever)"},fv=true}
E["quest:97287"] = {t="quest",n="Shrewd Negotiations",z="alterac",s="Magus Wordeen Voidglare praises your infiltration of the mages' city, and says the time has come to be more negotiatory. You are to carry the arcane mote you acquired to Archmage Celindra in Dalaran.",h="Magus Wordeen Voidglare praises your infiltration of the mages' city, and says the time has come to be more...",sec={{t="Time to Negotiate",b="Magus Wordeen Voidglare admits that no place on Azeroth rivals the Kirin Tor for knowledge of the arcane, and that even Wordeen's own brilliant work pales beside their ancient wisdom. He thinks it high time the Horde was granted access to their exclusive order. You are to carry the mote you acquired to Archmage Celindra in Dalaran, for Wordeen is sure the Kirin Tor will give anything to get it back.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends you to negotiate with Dalaran?",a="Magus Wordeen Voidglare, who wants to be more negotiatory after your infiltration of the city.",al={"who gives shrewd negotiations","wordeen voidglare","quest giver shrewd negotiations"}},{q="Who are you sent to speak with?",a="Archmage Celindra, in Dalaran.",al={"who do i talk to","celindra location","where is celindra"}},{q="What leverage do you carry?",a="The arcane mote you acquired. Wordeen is sure the Kirin Tor will give anything to have it back.",al={"what is the mote","bargaining chip","arcane mote"}},{q="Why does Wordeen Voidglare want to deal with Dalaran?",a="Wordeen admits no place on Azeroth rivals the Kirin Tor for knowledge of the arcane, and thinks it is time the Horde was granted access to their exclusive order.",al={"why negotiate with kirin tor","wordeen motive","why dalaran"}}},kw={"alterac mountains","arcane mote","archmage celindra","dalaran","kirin tor","shrewd negotiations","wordeen voidglare"},rel={"subzone:dalaran","zone:alterac"},m={start="Magus Wordeen Voidglare",["end"]="Archmage Celindra",level="33",faction="Horde",id=97287},src={"Shrewd Negotiations"},fv=true}
E["subzone:alterac-mountains"] = {t="subzone",n="Alterac Mountains",z="alterac",s="The Alterac Mountains are a rugged, snow-capped range rising directly above the rolling pastures of Hillsbrad. Once the heart of a proud human kingdom, the slopes now harbor ruined settlements, bandit factions, and dangerous wilderness where travelers rarely walk unguarded.",h="The Alterac Mountains are a rugged, snow-capped range rising directly above the rolling pastures of Hillsbrad.",sec={{t="A Fallen Realm",b="Long before the hills fell into chaos, these highlands formed the sovereign nation of Alterac, one of the seven kingdoms born from ancient Arathor. That legacy shattered during the Second War when King Aiden Perenolde struck a clandestine pact with the Old Horde, allowing orcish forces passage through the peaks in exchange for his kingdom's safety. The Alliance of Lordaeron uncovered the betrayal and deposed Perenolde, leaving the region fractured by martial law and territorial disputes.",sp=0},{t="Wilderness and Bandits",b="Following the devastation of the Third War, the mountains collapsed into complete lawlessness. The disinherited nobles of the realm banded together to form the Syndicate, operating out of the ruins of Strahnbrad and plotting to reclaim their lost dominion through sabotage and assassination. Between ruthless Crushridge ogres occupying the shattered capital, marauding gnolls, and the shattered magical ruins around Dalaran, the passes of Alterac remain some of the most perilous pathways in Lordaeron.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What kingdom used to rule these mountains?",a="The human kingdom of Alterac held these mountains for generations after the splintering of the Empire of Arathor. Its capital sat among the highest peaks, commanding the roads between Lordaeron, Dalaran, and the Arathi highlands until its fall during the Second War.",al={"who owned alterac","what was alterac","alterac kingdom lore"},it="history"},{q="Why is Alterac in ruins?",a="During the Second War, King Aiden Perenolde betrayed the Alliance of Lordaeron by assisting the Horde. When the treason was exposed, Alliance armies crushed Alterac's forces and deposed the crown. With no legitimate ruler and subsequent devastation from the Third War, the nation collapsed into rubble.",al={"what happened to alterac","who destroyed alterac","ruins of alterac backstory"},it="ruin"},{q="Who are the Syndicate lurking in the hills?",a="The Syndicate is an outlaw syndicate made up of former Alteraci nobility and their retainers. Led by Aliden Perenolde, they employ brigands, assassins, and rogue mercenaries to destabilize the region in hopes of violently restoring their kingdom.",al={"who is the syndicate","what is the syndicate","why are there bandits in alterac"},it="people"},{q="What threats wander the snowy peaks?",a="Travelers brave enough to climb the slopes must contend with the brutal Crushridge ogres, packs of Highland gnolls, scavenging kobolds, and opportunistic Syndicate brigands patrolling the passes.",al={"what lives in alterac","alterac monsters","threats in alterac"},it="danger"},{q="What are the Alterac Mountains?",a="The Alterac Mountains are a rugged, snow-capped range rising in central Lordaeron just north of the Hillsbrad Foothills. Once the sovereign territory of the human kingdom of Alterac, these heights held fortified cities, mountain keeps, and remote valleys. Today, the nation is broken and its towns lie shattered in the snow, leaving the freezing peaks a battleground for lingering outcasts, warring clans, and predatory monsters.",al={"what is alterac mountains","alterac mountains lore","alterac region overview"},it="place",add="e4635e9a"},{q="Who rules the Alterac Mountains today?",a="No legitimate government holds the Alterac Mountains. The kingdom collapsed after its treason in the Second War, and whatever order remained vanished during the Scourge's onslaught. Today, the Syndicate—dispossessed human nobles and outlaws led by the Perenolde bloodline—claims ancestral rights to the ruins. However, they violently contend with brutish Crushridge ogres, wandering undead, and entrenched Frostwolf orcs hidden in the high valleys.",al={"who controls alterac","who lives in alterac mountains","alterac leadership"},it="residents",add="858b3945"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, Alterac stands as a bitter monument to betrayal, where Perenolde's treachery nearly doomed humanity during the Second War.",["class:Rogue"]="The mountain passes are rife with Syndicate agents and hired cutthroats, making the hills a prime testing ground for survival and counter-espionage."},kw={"alterac","crushridge","hillsbrad","mountains","perenolde","strahnbrad","syndicate"},rel={"zone:hillsbrad","zone:alterac","subzone:ruins-of-alterac","subzone:strahnbrad","topic:alterac-kingdom","topic:syndicate","topic:alliance-of-lordaeron","subzone:dalaran"},src={"Alterac Mountains"}}
E["subzone:alterac-mountains-classic"] = {t="subzone",n="Alterac Mountains (Classic)",z="alterac",s="The Alterac Mountains are a rugged, overcast highland rising sharply north of Hillsbrad Foothills, crowned with permanent snow and jagged peaks. Once the home of the human kingdom of Alterac and the scholarly redoubts of Dalaran, the region now lies largely in ruins, fought over by brutal ogres, noble-born bandits, and the opposing armies of Alterac Valley.",h="The Alterac Mountains are a rugged, overcast highland rising sharply north of Hillsbrad Foothills, crowned...",sec={{t="A Shattered Highland",b="Rising high above the Hillsbrad lowlands, the Alterac Mountains are a harsh realm of rain, pine, and high-altitude snow. Once anchored by three major human powers—the mountain kingdom of Alterac, the magocracy of Dalaran, and the fortified town of Strahnbrad—the region collapsed under betrayal and war. Today, the ruined capital of Alterac is squatted by the Crushridge ogres, Strahnbrad is occupied by outlaws, and among the shattered remnants of Dalaran its surviving wizards work tirelessly to restore their ruined sanctuary.",sp=0},{t="Bandits, Beasts, and War",b="Beyond the indigenous mountain lions and yeti that stalk the frostbitten ridges, the uplands are contested by desperate mortal factions. The Syndicate—dispossessed human nobles turned brigands—wield blade and ambush from old estates and foothill encampments, clashing incessantly with the encroaching ogres. Meanwhile, deep passes leading into the high crags serve as staging camps for the bloody war between the Stormpike Expedition and the Frostwolf Clan over the hidden reaches of Alterac Valley.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What happened to the kingdom of Alterac?",a="Alterac fell into disgrace during the Second War when its ruler, King Aiden Perenolde, betrayed the Grand Alliance to aid the Horde. Following the war, the kingdom was dismantled. Bereft of leadership, its cities crumbled, Strahnbrad fell to ruin, and its capital was overrun by the brutish Crushridge ogres.",al={"why is alterac in ruins","who ruled alterac","fall of alterac"}},{q="Who are the Syndicate bandits in the mountains?",a="The Syndicate is an outlaw organization made up primarily of former Alterac nobility and their retainers. Having lost their land, status, and wealth after Alterac's betrayal, they took to espionage, assassination, and highway robbery in an attempt to reclaim the lands they believe are rightfully theirs.",al={"who is the syndicate","why are there rogues in alterac","alterac bandits"}},{q="What is the massive purple dome on the lake shore?",a="No dome stands over Dalaran today. After the city was razed by the demon lord Archimonde during the Third War, the surviving Kirin Tor mages raised a violet shield over its ruins, but they removed it early in the reconstruction and now rebuild their devastated towers in the open.",al={"purple bubble in alterac","what is dalaran bubble","magical shield dalaran"}},{q="How do you reach Alterac Mountains?",a="Travelers typically enter on foot from the Hillsbrad Foothills, taking the northern roads leading out of Tarren Mill or north of Southshore. Alternatively, daring swimmers can cross southeast over Lordamere Lake from the shores of Silverpine Forest or the outskirts of the Undercity.",al={"how to get to alterac","alterac entrance","path to alterac"}}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="Tucked away in a secluded mountain valley on the border of Alterac sits Ravenholdt Manor, the historic headquarters of the guild of thieves and assassins led by Lord Jorach Ravenholdt.",["faction:Alliance"]="The Alliance maintains a forward outpost in these frozen hills under Lieutenant Haggerdin, recruiting stalwart fighters to reinforce the dwarven Stormpike Guard in Alterac Valley."},kw={"alterac mountains","alterac valley","crushridge ogres","dalaran","lordamere","ruins of alterac","strahnbrad","syndicate","uplands"},rel={"zone:alterac","subzone:ruins-of-alterac","subzone:strahnbrad","subzone:dalaran","subzone:ravenholdt-manor","topic:alterac-kingdom","topic:syndicate","zone:hillsbrad"},src={"Alterac Mountains (Classic)"}}
E["subzone:dalaran"] = {t="subzone",n="Dalaran",z="alterac",s="Dalaran was once the shining magocratic capital of the Kirin Tor, nestled on the southern shore of Lordamere Lake. Shattered by the Scourge and the demon lord Archimonde during the Third War, its surviving magi are rebuilding the city, having removed its protective violet shield early in the reconstruction.",h="Dalaran was once the shining magocratic capital of the Kirin Tor, nestled on the southern shore of Lordamere...",sec={{t="Fall of the Magocracy",b="Founded after the ancient Troll Wars by sorcerers of the Arathorian Empire, Dalaran stood for centuries as humanity's premier sanctuary for arcane study. Under the leadership of the Council of Six, the Kirin Tor amassed vast magical archives and guarded powerful artifacts within the Violet Citadel. That age of splendor ended abruptly during the Third War. The traitor prince Arthas led the Scourge through the city gates to seize the Book of Medivh, and soon after, the demon lord Archimonde crushed Dalaran's soaring spires into rubble.",sp=0},{t="Rebuilding the Magocracy",b="In the aftermath of the Legion's defeat, the surviving wizards of the Kirin Tor returned to their devastated homeland. Refusing to surrender their ancestral ground to the Scourge or scavengers, they erected an impassable, shimmering violet barrier over the city's heart. The shield has since been removed, though reconstruction continues. The magi continue rebuilding their fallen sanctuary, and Archmage Ansirem Runeweaver can be found in the Violet Citadel.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What became of Dalaran's protective shield?",a="The Kirin Tor erected a magical shield over Dalaran after its destruction in the Third War. The shield has since been removed, and the city is still being rebuilt.",al={"purple bubble","purple shield alterac","what is the dome","dalaran dome"}},{q="Can players enter Dalaran?",a="Yes, while reconstruction is still underway, and Archmage Ansirem Runeweaver resides in the Violet Citadel. The Kirin Tor side with the Alliance, though: the Horde is Hated by them and attacked on sight in the city, but Horde groups can still run the City of Dalaran dungeon.",al={"can i get inside dalaran","how to enter dalaran","get past dalaran shield"}},{q="Who destroyed Dalaran?",a="Dalaran was attacked by Prince Arthas and his Scourge army, who stole the Book of Medivh from its vaults. Shortly after, the demon lord Archimonde summoned dark sorcery to pulverize the city into ruins.",al={"how did dalaran fall","who blew up dalaran","why is dalaran in ruins"}},{q="Who rules Dalaran?",a="The city is governed by the Kirin Tor, an elite magocratic order led by a ruling assembly known as the Council of Six.",al={"who runs dalaran","dalaran leadership","who leads kirin tor"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="Dalaran is the historical cradle of human and high elven wizardry. Seeing its legendary spires still being rebuilt serves as a solemn reminder of the devastating losses mages suffered in the Third War.",["faction:Alliance"]="Dalaran was one of the seven founding kingdoms of the original Alliance of Lordaeron, and the Kirin Tor is rebuilding its devastated capital."},kw={"alterac","archimonde","council of six","dalaran","dome","kirin tor","lordamere","shield","violet citadel"},rel={"zone:alterac","subzone:lordamere-lake","topic:third-war","topic:scourge","topic:burning-legion","topic:lordaeron"},src={"Dalaran"}}
E["subzone:dandred-s-fold"] = {t="subzone",n="Dandred's Fold",z="alterac",s="Dandred's Fold is a secluded farmstead and manor tucked along the misty northwestern shores of Lordamere Lake in the Alterac Mountains. Now overrun by the Syndicate, it serves as a secure hideout for Lord Aliden Perenolde and his co-conspirators. Both the Horde and the Alliance keep a watchful eye on this lakefront retreat for very different reasons.",h="Dandred's Fold is a secluded farmstead and manor tucked along the misty northwestern shores of Lordamere Lake...",sec={{t="A Noble Safe Haven Fallen to Outlaws",b="Perched on the western edge of the Uplands with private access to the waters of Lordamere Lake, Dandred's Fold was once a tranquil country estate, likely owned by an Alteraci noble named Dandred. In the aftermath of the kingdom's fall, the estate transformed into a fortified enclave for the Syndicate. Syndicate assassins and enforcers now patrol its fences and docks, shielding the fallen nobility from the eyes of Southshore authorities and the Forsaken across the lake.",sp=0},{t="A Nexus of Intrigues",b="Behind the manor's closed doors, dangerous conspiracies brew. Lord Aliden Perenolde, the recognized leader of the Syndicate, uses Dandred's Fold as his base of operations alongside his mistress, Elysa. Yet the outlaws are not alone; a rogue Shadow Council orc named Nagaz of the Argus Wake has also embedded himself here, brokering dark pacts with the human brigands. This dangerous alliance makes Dandred's Fold a target for Southshore's magistrates and Horde champions alike.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who controls Dandred's Fold?",a="The estate is occupied by the Syndicate, an aristocratic criminal network led by the deposed nobles of Alterac. Syndicate assassins and enforcers guard the grounds, serving under Lord Aliden Perenolde.",al={"who is at dandreds fold","who lives at dandred's fold","dandreds fold mobs"},it="residents"},{q="Why does the Horde care about this estate?",a="The Horde targets the manor to strike down Lord Aliden Perenolde and retrieve a stolen keepsake: the heirloom necklace that once belonged to Taretha Foxton, Thrall's childhood savior and confidante.",al={"horde dandreds fold","why horde go to dandreds fold"},sp=1,it="conflict",bt={"q533.6"}},{q="Why does the Alliance send adventurers here?",a="Magistrate Henry Maleb of Southshore directs Alliance agents here to eliminate Nagaz, a dangerous member of the Argus Wake cult who is colluding with the Syndicate outlaws.",al={"alliance dandreds fold","magistrate maleb quest dandreds fold"}},{q="Who was Dandred?",a="The identity of Dandred is unrecorded. The estate bears the name, but no confirmed account identifies its original owner.",al={"who is dandred","dandred lore"},it="name"},{q="What is Dandred's Fold?",a="Dandred's Fold is a secluded farm and manor perched on the western Uplands of the Alterac Mountains, bordering the misty shores of Lordamere Lake. Once a peaceful noble estate, it now serves as a fortified haven and operational base for the Syndicate.",al={"what is dandreds fold","dandreds fold alterac","about dandreds fold"},it="place",add="e469c160"},{q="What happened at Dandred's Fold?",a="Following the collapse of the Kingdom of Alterac, this lakeside farm fell into the hands of the Syndicate. Lord Aliden Perenolde turned the isolated manor into a personal stronghold and retreat, forging dangerous ties with shadowy organizations like the Argus Wake.",al={"dandreds fold history","what happened to dandreds fold"},it="history",add="b8b5cedb"},{q="Is Dandred's Fold dangerous?",a="It is extremely hazardous for lone travelers. The grounds are guarded by skilled Syndicate enforcers, stealthy cutthroats, and covert agents of the Argus Wake, all fiercely loyal to Lord Aliden Perenolde and hostile to outside intruders.",al={"is dandreds fold dangerous","dandred fold danger","who is at dandreds fold"},it="danger",add="fc1f4fab"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For the Horde, infiltrating Dandred's Fold is deeply personal. Warchief Thrall seeks the retrieval of Taretha Foxton's necklace.",["faction:Alliance"]="The Alliance cannot tolerate an alliance between human outlaws and the demonic Argus Wake, prompting Magistrate Henry Maleb to order surgical strikes against the estate."},kw={"aliden perenolde","argus wake","dandred's fold","dandreds fold","elysa","lordamere lake","nagaz","syndicate","uplands"},rel={"topic:syndicate","zone:alterac","npc:magistrate-henry-maleb","subzone:uplands","subzone:lordamere-lake","subzone:misty-shore","topic:alterac-kingdom","topic:alliance"},src={"Dandred's Fold"}}
E["subzone:lordamere-internment-camp"] = {t="subzone",n="Lordamere Internment Camp",z="alterac",s="Lordamere Internment Camp is a former Second War detention facility perched on the heights overlooking Dalaran. Once built to confine lethargic orcs, the camp is now occupied by surviving Dalaran magi and guards alongside a treacherous band of Forsaken defectors.",h="Lordamere Internment Camp is a former Second War detention facility perched on the heights overlooking...",sec={{t="From Prison to Research Outpost",b="Following the Second War, the Alliance constructed internment camps across the northern kingdoms to contain the defeated orcish Horde. Lordamere was unique as the sole camp established within the Alterac Mountains, placed under Dalaran's jurisdiction. With the orcs long since liberated or fled, the camp today functions under Warden Belamoore as an outpost for Dalaran remnants studying dangerous magical relics.",sp=0},{t="Forsaken Defectors",b="The camp has become entangled in the politics of Lordaeron's undead. Four Forsaken renegades—Kegan Darkmar and his compatriots—stole powerful Bloodstone artifacts from the Undercity and fled here, trading them to Warden Belamoore in exchange for sanctuary behind Dalaran's lines. The magi gladly accepted the artifacts for arcane study, while executors in Tarren Mill dispatch loyal Horde operatives to hunt the defectors down and recover the stolen bloodstones before Dalaran unlocks their power.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What was this camp originally built for?",a="It was established by the Alliance after the Second War to imprison captive orcs who had succumbed to lethargy after losing their demonic bloodlust. Dalaran manned the watchtowers and maintained oversight over the camp due to its close proximity to the magi's city.",al={"internment camp history","why is there a camp here","what is this place"}},{q="Who controls the camp right now?",a="Warden Belamoore and a detachment of Dalaran guards and magi hold the camp. Though Dalaran itself was heavily damaged, these survivors continue their research from the fortified hilltop.",al={"who lives here","who runs the camp","who is warden belamoore"}},{q="Why are there undead Forsaken inside the camp?",a="They are deserters from the Undercity led by Kegan Darkmar. Having betrayed Queen Sylvanas and stolen sacred Bloodstone artifacts, they traded the relics to Warden Belamoore in exchange for Dalaran's protection against Forsaken retribution.",al={"undead here","kegan darkmar","forsaken deserters"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="The deserters holed up in Lordamere represent a direct betrayal of the Dark Lady. Hunting down Kegan Darkmar and recovering the Bloodstones is vital to keeping Forsaken secrets out of human hands.",["race:Orc"]="For orcs, visiting this camp is a grim reminder of the post-Second War era when thousands of their kin withered in captivity before Thrall rallied their people."},kw={"alterac","belamoore","bloodstone","dalaran","internment","kegan darkmar","lordamere","orcs"},rel={"zone:alterac","subzone:dalaran","topic:second-war","topic:forsaken","topic:horde"},src={"Lordamere Internment Camp"}}
E["subzone:misty-shore"] = {t="subzone",n="Misty Shore",z="alterac",s="Misty Shore is the quiet lakeshore of the Alterac Mountains, skirting the eastern shore of Lordamere Lake. Stretching between Dandred's Fold and the perimeter of Dalaran, it offers wide, foggy views of the Dawning Isles and the sinister silhouette of Fenris Keep.",h="Misty Shore is the quiet lakeshore of the Alterac Mountains, skirting the eastern shore of Lordamere Lake.",sec={{t="A Fog-Shrouded Waterline",b="Running along Lordamere Lake, the Misty Shore stretches between Dandred's Fold and Dalaran. Thick, damp air regularly drifts off the lake, obscuring snapping turtles and the occasional zealous fanatic who wanders down from regional strongholds.",sp=0},{t="Watching the Lake",b="From the banks of the Misty Shore, travelers look out across the waters toward the Dawning Isles and the imposing shadow of Fenris Keep. Because of its vantage point across Lordamere Lake and its proximity to both Dalaran and Scarlet-controlled pockets, travelers along the bank often keep a low profile to avoid unwanted attention.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Misty Shore located?",a="Misty Shore lies in the Alterac Mountains, running along the eastern shore of Lordamere Lake between Dandred's Fold and the Dalaran perimeter.",al={"misty shore location","where is misty shore","misty shore map"},it="place"},{q="What can be seen across the water from here?",a="Looking across the waters of Lordamere Lake, you can see the Dawning Isles and the looming structure of Fenris Keep out in the fog.",al={"what is across the water","misty shore view","lake view"}},{q="What threats are typically found along the shore?",a="The shoreline is inhabited by lake beasts like snapjaw turtles, but travelers also risk encountering zealots aligned with the Scarlet Crusade or scouts roaming from neighboring farmsteads and ruins.",al={"misty shore danger","enemies at misty shore","creatures on misty shore"},it="threat"},{q="What is Misty Shore?",a="Misty Shore is a quiet, fog-shrouded stretch of shoreline bordering the eastern shore of Lordamere Lake in the Alterac Mountains. It extends roughly between Dandred's Fold and the perimeter of Dalaran, offering a clear view across the lake toward the Dawning Isles and the distant towers of Fenris Keep.",al={"what is misty shore","about misty shore","misty shore overview"},it="place",add="140433c1"},{q="Is Misty Shore dangerous?",a="While it appears placid at first glance, the shore is far from safe. The waters and banks teem with aggressive snapjaw turtles, and travelers must watch for hostile humans aligned with the Scarlet Crusade who patrol nearby, attacking anyone they perceive as tainted or trespassers.",al={"how dangerous is misty shore","misty shore dangers","is misty shore safe"},it="danger",add="fbe1f33b"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="The shores of Lordamere Lake provide an abundant hunting ground for snapping turtles, yielding tender meat valuable to cooks traveling through Alterac.",["faction:Horde"]="The misty bank provides a natural approach between the Forsaken-held lands near Tarren Mill and the northern lakeshore, keeping travelers sheltered from open patrols."},kw={"alterac mountains","dandred's fold","dawning isles","fenris keep","lordamere lake","misty shore","turtles"},rel={"subzone:lordamere-lake","zone:alterac","subzone:dandred-s-fold","subzone:fenris-isle","subzone:fenris-keep","subzone:dawning-isles","topic:scarlet-crusade"},src={"Misty Shore"}}
E["subzone:ruins-of-alterac"] = {t="subzone",n="Ruins of Alterac",z="alterac",s="The snow-covered Ruins of Alterac are all that remain of Alterac City, once the proud mountain capital of the Kingdom of Alterac. Cast out of the Alliance and put under martial law after King Aiden Perenolde's treason during the Second War, the shattered stronghold is now overrun by the brutish Crushridge ogres.",h="The snow-covered Ruins of Alterac are all that remain of Alterac City, once the proud mountain capital of the...",sec={{t="A Kingdom's Betrayal",b="Alterac was once an independent human realm carved out of the old Arathor empire, perched high on the trade routes through the mountains. During the Second War, fearing destruction at the hands of the invading Old Horde, King Aiden Perenolde secretly struck a pact with the orcs. When the betrayal was uncovered following the fighting at Caer Darrow, the Alliance of Lordaeron retaliated swiftly. King Terenas Menethil II put the city under martial law and deposed Perenolde. The grand fortifications, church, and palace fell into disrepair as the populace fled or turned to outlawry.",sp=0},{t="The Ogre Occupation",b="While surviving Alteraci nobles and rogue soldiers formed the Syndicate to wage guerrilla campaigns from towns like Strahnbrad, they lost their ancestral capital entirely. Today, the Crushridge ogres under Mug'thol dwell among the broken ramparts, palace halls, and wrecked ballistae. Neither the Syndicate nor the human defenders of Southshore have managed to reclaim the fallen city, leaving its crumbling towers and abandoned vaults as dangerous territory for treasure hunters and scavengers.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why was Alterac destroyed?",a="During the Second War, King Aiden Perenolde allied with the invading Orcish Horde to spare his kingdom. The Alliance of Lordaeron discovered the treason, invaded Alterac City, dismantled its defenses, and placed the kingdom under martial law.",al={"why is alterac in ruins","what happened to alterac city","fall of alterac"},it="ruin"},{q="Who lives in the ruins now?",a="The Crushridge ogres, led by Mug'thol, have overtaken the palace, walls, and snowed-in courtyards. In addition, an enterprising goblin alchemy vendor named Bro'kin sits quietly atop the northern ramparts.",al={"who controls alterac ruins","alterac ogres","who is in alterac"},it="residents"},{q="What is the Syndicate's connection to this place?",a="The Syndicate is largely composed of former Alteraci aristocracy and soldiers who lost their lands after the kingdom was dissolved. While they bitterly yearn to reclaim Alterac, they were driven from the capital itself by the Crushridge ogres and now operate out of outposts like Strahnbrad.",al={"does the syndicate live here","syndicate alterac connection"},it="ties"},{q="Why do Alliance adventurers come here?",a="Alliance soldiers from Southshore offer bounties on the hostile Crushridge ogres who raid the roads, while nobles in the south, such as Count Remington Ridgewell, send agents into the ruins to recover lost family heirlooms like the Perenolde Tiara.",al={"alliance quests alterac ruins","crushridge bounty"},it="motive"},{q="Why is the Horde interested in these ruins?",a="Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and the Forsaken take an active interest in the artifacts scattered across the fallen human kingdom, dispatching champions into the ogre-infested stronghold to secure relics of power such as the Crown of Will.",al={"horde quests alterac ruins","sylvanas alterac"},it="purpose"},{q="What is the Ruins of Alterac?",a="These snowbound stone walls and broken parapets are all that remain of Alterac City, once the proud mountain capital of the human Kingdom of Alterac. Founded thousands of years ago following the expansion of Arathor, the city guarded the vital trade routes winding through the mountains until its king's treachery brought about its downfall during the Second War.",al={"what is ruins of alterac","ruins of alterac overview","alterac city"},it="place",add="46d22466"},{q="What happened to Alterac City during the Second War?",a="During the Second War, King Aiden Perenolde struck a clandestine pact with the invading Orcish Horde to spare his realm. When the Alliance of Lordaeron discovered Alterac's treason, Alliance forces marched upon the mountain kingdom, razing the capital and placing the remnants under martial law. Deposed and disgraced, Perenolde was imprisoned, leaving the kingdom shattered and abandoned.",al={"alterac city history","what happened at alterac","fall of alterac"},it="history",add="967fd086"},{q="How dangerous are the Ruins of Alterac?",a="Extremely dangerous for the unprepared. The Crushridge ogres have made the snow-covered streets and dilapidated halls their home, fiercely defending their territory against any who trespass. Compounding the peril, the ruins occasionally draw the attention of the ruthless Syndicate and wandering undead, leaving the mountain passes treacherous and fraught with ambush.",al={"is ruins of alterac dangerous","ruins of alterac threats","alterac city dangers"},it="danger",add="fd0078c8"},{q="Why is this place called the Ruins of Alterac?",a="The site takes its name from the ancient human kingdom and city of Alterac that once stood here. Following the kingdom's dissolution and the physical devastation wrought during the Second War, nothing survived of the grand capital except cracked masonry, shattered gates, and crumbling towers, reducing the once-mighty seat of power to a mere ruined landmark.",al={"why called ruins of alterac","ruins of alterac name origin"},it="name",add="fbcb07c6"}},ang={["race:Human"]="For humans of the Alliance, the ruins are a somber reminder of human weakness and treason during the Second War, where Perenolde's cowardice broke the brotherhood of the Seven Kingdoms.",["faction:Horde"]="The fallen city stands as an echo of the Old Horde's former alliances, but today offers opportunities for the Forsaken to scavenge magical relics from the distracted Crushridge ogres."},kw={"alterac city","bro'kin","crushridge","mug'thol","perenolde","ruins of alterac","strahnbrad","syndicate"},rel={"topic:alterac-kingdom","topic:syndicate","zone:alterac","subzone:strahnbrad","quest:543","topic:alliance-of-lordaeron","topic:terenas-menethil-ii","topic:second-war"},src={"Ruins of Alterac"}}
E["subzone:uplands"] = {t="subzone",n="Uplands",z="alterac",s="The Uplands is a rolling, elevated territory in the northeastern Alterac Mountains that once served as the agricultural heartland of the fallen Kingdom of Alterac. Following the kingdom's collapse, the fertile hills fell entirely under the sway of the Syndicate. Today, the criminal organization maintains its strongest base of power here, fortifying multiple encampments across the slopes.",h="The Uplands is a rolling, elevated territory in the northeastern Alterac Mountains that once served as the...",sec={{t="Breadbasket to Bandit Stronghold",b="Before the Second War broke Alterac apart, the hills of the Uplands were celebrated as the kingdom's breadbasket, providing grain and livestock to feed its mountain fortresses. When the core of the realm fell to ruin and infamy, the farming estates were abandoned by honest folk. In their place rose the Syndicate, led by dispossessed Alterac nobles and cutthroats determined to reclaim their stolen inheritance through force. The Uplands now represents the Syndicate's most heavily concentrated territory in the region, dotted with camps, patrols, and outposts like Dandred's Fold along its western borders.",sp=0},{t="A Seat of Shadows",b="Because the Syndicate commands these hills in force, high-ranking conspirators often oversee operations from the Uplands. Figures such as Baron Vardus, aligned with the shadowy leadership steering the remnants of Alterac's nobility, coordinate brigand movements, raids on neighboring valleys, and resistance against both the Alliance and Horde. Travelers crossing into the northeastern ridges face immediate hostility from entrenched highwaymen who view the entire range as their sovereign soil.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What was the Uplands originally used for?",a="The Uplands was historically the primary agricultural region of the Kingdom of Alterac. Its rolling hills served as the kingdom's breadbasket before war and betrayal brought about the nation's downfall.",al={"uplands history","what used to be here","uplands purpose"},it="history"},{q="Who controls the Uplands now?",a="The Uplands is held by the Syndicate. Alterac's former nobility and their network of bandits have established multiple camps throughout these hills, making it the area where their presence is strongest.",al={"who lives in uplands","who holds the uplands","uplands factions"},it="residents"},{q="Where is the Uplands located?",a="The Uplands spans the northeastern highlands of the Alterac Mountains, bordering Dandred's Fold along its western edge.",al={"uplands location","where is uplands","how to find uplands"},it="place"},{q="Who is Baron Vardus?",a="Baron Vardus is an influential noble and leader within the Syndicate who oversees operations in the Uplands, directing the bandits and conspirators seeking to reclaim Alterac.",al={"baron vardus lore","who is vardus","uplands baron"}},{q="Why is the Uplands ruined and abandoned?",a="The Uplands once flourished as the breadbasket of the kingdom of Alterac, filled with fertile fields and homesteads. When the kingdom collapsed following its betrayal during the Second War, its heartland was shattered. Without the kingdom's protection, the agricultural heart of the region withered and was overrun by criminals, leaving ruins like Dandred's Fold in its wake.",al={"why is uplands ruined","what happened to uplands farms","why is uplands abandoned"},it="ruin",add="35db727f"},{q="Is the Uplands dangerous?",a="It is exceptionally dangerous. The Uplands serves as the primary stronghold of the Syndicate, harboring their heaviest concentration of fighters anywhere in the mountains. Wandering bandits, outlaws, and rogue nobles patrol the hills, fiercely guarding their camps against any outsiders who intrude on their territory.",al={"is uplands dangerous","uplands danger","how dangerous is uplands"},it="danger",add="4211f63f"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="The Uplands serves as the primary seat of power for the Syndicate, making it a crucial study in how displaced nobility turned an entire regional network of bandits into an organized, lethal cartel.",["race:Human"]="These hills are a grim reminder of Alterac's fall; what was once a flourishing agricultural breadbasket for humanity is now choked with cutthroats and ruined ambitions."},kw={"alterac","baron vardus","breadbasket","dandred's fold","mountains","syndicate","uplands"},rel={"zone:alterac","topic:syndicate","topic:alterac-kingdom","subzone:dandred-s-fold"},src={"Uplands"}}
E["zone:alterac"] = {t="zone",n="Alterac Mountains",z="alterac",s="The Alterac Mountains are a cold, ruined highland in central Lordaeron, once home to the treacherous human kingdom of Alterac and the scholarly magocracy of Dalaran. Today, the snow-dusted crags are overrun by the Crushridge ogres, the aristocratic bandits of the Syndicate, and remnant arcane forces. Travelers venture from nearby foothill settlements and the rebuilding city of Dalaran.",h="The Alterac Mountains are a cold, ruined highland in central Lordaeron, once home to the treacherous human...",sec={{t="The Fallen Kingdom",b="During the Second War, Alterac was one of the Seven Kingdoms of humanity, but King Aiden Perenolde betrayed the Alliance of Lordaeron to side with the Old Horde, hoping to preserve his realm. His treachery was discovered and stamped out, fracturing the nation into disputed borderlands. Following the kingdom's dissolution and the horrors of the Third War, Alterac's grand stone capital was reduced to rubble. Today, the Ruins of Alterac are occupied by the brutal Crushridge ogres, led by Mug'thol, while the surviving human nobility organized into the Syndicate, a vicious criminal syndicate fighting to reclaim their lost estates by force.",sp=0},{t="The Rebuilding City",b="On the western edge of the mountains, along the shores of Lordamere Lake, sits what remains of the Kirin Tor's great city-state of Dalaran. Devastated by the demon lord Archimonde during the Third War, Dalaran's surviving magi threw up a massive, opaque violet dome of protective magic over the ruins, but it has since been removed, and they rebuild the city in the open. The Kirin Tor continue rebuilding their sanctum, and Archmage Ansirem Runeweaver can be found within the Violet Citadel.",sp=0},{t="Frontiers of Conflict",b="Adventurers often venture into the peaks using Southshore or Tarren Mill as staging grounds. Beyond the wandering yetis, mountain lions, and Syndicate footpads, the region's greatest conflict churns beneath the snow line. Deep within the mountain passes lies Alterac Valley, where the dwarven Stormpike Guard have clashed with the reclusive Frostwolf clan of orcs over ancient territorial and mining rights.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What happened to the Kingdom of Alterac?",a="During the Second War, King Aiden Perenolde betrayed the Alliance to aid the Horde. Lordaeron and Stromgarde crushed the treason, occupying the land. When the Scourge tore through Lordaeron in the Third War, what remained of Alterac collapsed into anarchy, leaving its ruined capital to the Crushridge ogres.",al={"why is alterac destroyed","what happened to perenolde","alterac kingdom lore"}},{q="Who are the Syndicate?",a="The Syndicate is an outlaw organization formed from the dispossessed nobility of Alterac. Led by former Alteraci royals such as Lord Aliden Perenolde, they employ cutthroats, highwaymen, and disgraced lords to terrorize the surrounding lands and drive out rivals, striving desperately to reclaim their ancestral domains.",al={"who is the syndicate","why are there human bandits in alterac","syndicate lore"}},{q="What happened to Dalaran's glowing dome?",a="After Archimonde devastated Dalaran during the Third War, the surviving Kirin Tor raised a protective magical shield over the ruins. The shield has since been removed, and the city is being rebuilt in the open. Archmage Ansirem Runeweaver now stands in the Violet Citadel.",al={"purple dome alterac","what is the violet bubble","dalaran shield"}},{q="Where can I find flight paths or safe inns in Alterac?",a="Southshore and Tarren Mill in the Hillsbrad Foothills are the usual staging grounds for expeditions into the snowy peaks. Dalaran on the western edge is open to Alliance travelers while the Kirin Tor rebuild it, though it has no flight master; the Horde is Hated by the Kirin Tor and attacked on sight in the city.",al={"alterac flight path","alterac inn","alterac quest hub"}},{q="What is Alterac Valley?",a="Alterac Valley is an isolated, snowy vale contested by the dwarven Stormpike Guard and the Frostwolf clan of orcs. The Stormpikes arrived on an archaeological expedition, which provoked an all-out territorial war with the Frostwolves who have lived peacefully in the valley since their exile in the First War.",al={"av entrance","frostwolf vs stormpike","where is alterac valley"}},{q="What is Ravenholdt Manor?",a="Hidden in an obscure mountain fold east of the main road lies Ravenholdt Manor, the secretive guildhall of the League of Assassins. Commanded by Lord Jorach Ravenholdt, it serves as a training ground and haven for skilled rogues from across Azeroth.",al={"where is ravenholdt","assassins manor alterac","thieves guild alterac"}}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="The hidden valley of Ravenholdt Manor nestles in the eastern cliffs of Alterac, offering elite contracts, lockpicking drills, and secret guild secrets under the eye of Lord Jorach Ravenholdt.",["class:Mage"]="Dalaran's rebuilding streets hum with residual arcane currents and busy Kirin Tor mages, serving as a solemn pilgrimage to the devastated heart of human spellcraft.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance travelers face the Crushridge ogres and Syndicate outlaws occupying the former kingdom.",["faction:Horde"]="The Frostwolf clan has made its home in the secluded mountains, while Forsaken agents out of Tarren Mill confront ogres and Syndicate outlaws.",["profession:Herbalism"]="The frozen crags of Alterac are renowned among herbalists as the only natural habitat for Wintersbite, an essential component in potent cold-weather concoctions."},kw={"alterac","crushridge","dalaran","perenolde","ravenholdt","strahnbrad","syndicate","uplands"},rel={"subzone:ruins-of-alterac","subzone:strahnbrad","subzone:ravenholdt-manor","topic:alterac-kingdom","topic:syndicate","zone:hillsbrad","npc:lord-jorach-ravenholdt"},src={"Alterac Mountains (Classic)","Alterac Mountains"}}
